---
/*
  One sprite for every mark on the page, inlined once in the layout.

  The brand marks are the single paths shipped by `simple-icons` (MIT), so a
  logo is the real one rather than an approximation of it — and no icon font,
  no request per logo, no layout shift while they arrive. LinkedIn no longer
  ships in that set, so its mark is drawn here to the same 24-unit grid.

  Telegram is the plane on its own rather than the plane knocked out of a disc:
  at 16 px the knockout closes up and the mark turns into a blob, while the
  silhouette still reads. It is scaled off its own bounding box to fill the
  grid, since the shipped path is sized for the disc it used to sit in.

  `b-mail` is not a brand and is drawn here, but it is built like the marks it
  stands next to: solid, filling the grid, with the flap cut out of the body
  rather than drawn on it, so it holds at the 16 px the chips use.

  `u-*` are this page's own interface icons: stroked at 1.6–1.9 so their weight
  sits with the text they stand next to.
*/
